          "z": 259
        }
      ],
      "residents": [
        {
          "id": "amos_haskell",
          "name": "Amos Haskell",
          "kind": "farmer",
          "home": "madeline_haskell_farm",
          "talk": [
            "Hay to Bayfield for the livery, potatoes for the camps. A living, just.",
            "The road to Big Bay runs past my fence. Plenty walk it these days.",
            "In February the ice road's the best road we have. Bayfield's an hour's walk."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "nils_nygaard",
          "name": "Nils Nygaard",
          "kind": "farmer",
          "home": "madeline_nygaard_farm",
          "talk": [
            "The old fur company's warehouse is down by the dock. Not much fur left to keep in it.",
            "My cows don't care who's in the papers. I do, a little."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pete_larsen",
          "name": "Pete Larsen",
          "kind": "fisherman",
          "home": "madeline_north_camp",
          "talk": [
            "Herring off the north end in the fall. I salt them here and take them down to the village.",
            "From up here you see every sail that rounds the point. I keep a tally."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "agnes_moreau",
          "name": "Agnes Moreau",
          "kind": "villager",
          "round": [
            {
              "x": 185,
              "z": 1430
            },
            {
              "x": 232,
              "z": 1452
            },
            {
              "x": 212,
              "z": 1500
            },
            {
              "x": 176,
              "z": 1394
            }
          ],
          "talk": [
            "The trading post buys and sells most anything. Ask at the counter.",
            "Father Chebul says Mass on Sunday at St. Joseph's. Everyone comes, sooner or later.",
            "The steamer brings the papers from Bayfield. We read about everyone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "frank_duval",
          "name": "Frank Duval",
          "kind": "fisherman",
          "round": [
            {
              "x": 115,
              "z": 1305
            },
            {
              "x": 122,
              "z": 1333
            },
            {
              "x": 128,
              "z": 1370
            }
          ],
          "talk": [
            "Fish dock's mine most mornings. Mind the nets on the planks.",
            "The Bayfield boats come over for our catch. They pay less than Duluth."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "reporting": "medium",
      "village": {
        "harbor": "harbor.la_pointe",
